{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_154028_53ecd5", "exit_code": 0, "text": "# Sales Battlecard: Aurora 14 vs. Vantage Pro 16\n\n## Positioning\nAurora 14 positions as the portable, AI-ready workstation for professionals who need upgradability and future-proof service. It trades raw screen size and GPU VRAM for superior AI performance, portability, and long-term value.\n\n## Aurora 14 Strengths\n1. **Upgradable Memory**: Supports up to 128 GB with user-upgradeable slots. Vantage Pro 16 is limited to 64 GB soldered RAM.\n2. **AI Performance**: Features a 60 TOPS NPU vs. 40 TOPS, providing greater headroom for running large local AI models.\n3. **Service**: Includes a 3-year on-site warranty, compared to Vantage's 1-year depot service.\n\n## Vantage Pro 16 Strengths\n1. **Screen**: Larger 16-inch display with a 165 Hz refresh rate, preferred for visualization tasks.\n2. **GPU VRAM**: Offers 24 GB of GPU memory vs. 16 GB, beneficial for large 3D scenes.\n\n## Objection Handling\n\n**Objection 1: \"Aurora is $300 more expensive.\"**\nResponse: The higher starting price reflects a premium 60 TOPS NPU for local AI, a 3-year on-site warranty, and user-upgradeable RAM. Vantage's lower price locks you into soldered 64 GB RAM.\n\n**Objection 2: \"I need 24 GB of VRAM for my 3D work.\"**\nResponse: Vantage Pro 16 does offer 24 GB VRAM, which is superior for large GPU-bound scenes. However, Aurora's upgradable memory and higher NPU throughput provide better long-term value for AI workflows.\n\n**Objection 3: \"The 16-inch screen on the Vantage is better for my work.\"**\nResponse: The Vantage's 16-inch IPS screen is indeed larger with a 165 Hz refresh rate. Aurora compensates with a lighter 1.65 kg chassis and up to 11 hours of battery life, making it easier to carry.\n\n## Discovery Question\n\"When you consider your workflow, do you prioritize immediate screen real estate, or do you need the ability to upgrade your memory later as your software demands grow?\"", "tokens": {"input": 791, "output": 515, "total": 5125, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 58956, "timestamp": 1790808087736}